{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00467",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.12,
      "end_seconds": 5.54,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "Doctor, I've brought them through. The observations are done, whenever you need them."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 6.11,
      "end_seconds": 8.87,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Okay, thanks. Hi, how can I help today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 10.47,
      "end_seconds": 22.84,
      "duration_seconds": 12.37,
      "text": "It's a burning pain in the upper tummy, mostly. My family kept telling me to get it checked. A neighbour of mine said I should see someone about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 23.47,
      "end_seconds": 25.73,
      "duration_seconds": 2.26,
      "text": "How long have you had it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 26.71,
      "end_seconds": 34.73,
      "duration_seconds": 8.02,
      "text": "For about a week, I'd say. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.22,
      "end_seconds": 43.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.81,
      "text": "Okay, give me more detail on it, whatever comes to mind."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.64,
      "end_seconds": 67.6,
      "duration_seconds": 20.96,
      "text": "Milk helps a bit. It's worse with spicy food. A four out of ten, I suppose. My sister suggested writing things down, but I forgot. And there's a sour taste in the mouth as well, two weeks now. I mean, as for sour taste in the mouth, I'd say moderate."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.15,
      "end_seconds": 72.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.21,
      "text": "Give me a second, I'm just scrolling back through your chart."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 72.98,
      "end_seconds": 73.83,
      "duration_seconds": 0.85,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 84.99,
      "end_seconds": 90.95,
      "duration_seconds": 5.96,
      "text": "Alright, I've got it. Have you had any vomiting blood, weight loss, jaundice or trouble swallowing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 92.38,
      "end_seconds": 94.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.21,
      "text": "Oh, nothing like that, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 95.76,
      "end_seconds": 98.19,
      "duration_seconds": 2.43,
      "text": "Right, have you had any fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 99.26,
      "end_seconds": 100.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "No. No fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.96,
      "end_seconds": 105.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.38,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 106.42,
      "end_seconds": 108.55,
      "duration_seconds": 2.13,
      "text": "No, uh, nothing there."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 109.56,
      "end_seconds": 112.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.85,
      "text": "One moment, the system's being slow today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.27,
      "end_seconds": 114.08,
      "duration_seconds": 0.81,
      "text": "That's alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 129.54,
      "end_seconds": 134.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.95,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. What about your general health, any conditions you're being treated for?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 135.68,
      "end_seconds": 152.29,
      "duration_seconds": 16.61,
      "text": "Hmm, yes, arthritis in my knees. I did try to ignore it for a while. Yes, acid reflux. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite. I took the morning off to come in today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.16,
      "end_seconds": 160.61,
      "duration_seconds": 7.45,
      "text": "So, yes, I can see the acid reflux in your file as well. Let me know if I'm going too fast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.11,
      "end_seconds": 163.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.3,
      "text": "No, uh, you're fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.49,
      "end_seconds": 166.68,
      "duration_seconds": 2.19,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 167.69,
      "end_seconds": 170.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.13,
      "text": "Not that I know, you know, no."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 172.14,
      "end_seconds": 175.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "Let me make a quick note of that before I forget."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 176.55,
      "end_seconds": 177.25,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 186.67,
      "end_seconds": 189.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Right, thanks for waiting. What about alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 190.9,
      "end_seconds": 194.37,
      "duration_seconds": 3.47,
      "text": "I have a couple of drinks on the weekend."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 194.68,
      "end_seconds": 195.61,
      "duration_seconds": 0.93,
      "text": "Do you smoke?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 196.36,
      "end_seconds": 199.27,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "I smoke, yes, around five a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.41,
      "end_seconds": 202.98,
      "duration_seconds": 2.57,
      "text": "Are you comfortable? Do you want some water?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.22,
      "end_seconds": 208.75,
      "duration_seconds": 4.53,
      "text": "Uh, yes, some water would be nice, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.45,
      "end_seconds": 213.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.91,
      "text": "Any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 214.1,
      "end_seconds": 221.19,
      "duration_seconds": 7.09,
      "text": "I had a hernia repair about five years back. I thought it would sort itself out, but it hasn't."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 221.76,
      "end_seconds": 226.36,
      "duration_seconds": 4.6,
      "text": "Is there anyone at home who can help you out if you need it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 227.18,
      "end_seconds": 237.47,
      "duration_seconds": 10.29,
      "text": "Yes, there's family around most evenings, and they've been very good about checking in, although they do worry more than they need to."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 238.23,
      "end_seconds": 241.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.87,
      "text": "Let's go through your medication. What are you taking?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 241.97,
      "end_seconds": 253.55,
      "duration_seconds": 11.58,
      "text": "I'm on pantoprazole, 40 milligrams, before breakfast for my acidity. I looked a few things up online, and that probably didn't help. Well, I take Gelusil, after meals."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 253.94,
      "end_seconds": 270.44,
      "duration_seconds": 16.5,
      "text": "Let me explain how I'm thinking about this. When someone has symptoms like these, we first look for the common and treatable causes, and only then for the rarer ones. That's why I'm going step by step rather than ordering everything at once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 271.08,
      "end_seconds": 272.74,
      "duration_seconds": 1.66,
      "text": "Okay, that makes sense."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 275.8,
      "end_seconds": 281.95,
      "duration_seconds": 6.15,
      "text": "Here are the numbers, doctor. Heart rate 84, blood pressure 113 over 82, SpO2 99 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 282.59,
      "end_seconds": 283.29,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.48,
      "end_seconds": 287.22,
      "duration_seconds": 2.74,
      "text": "Let me have a look at you now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 288.9,
      "end_seconds": 290.49,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "Look straight ahead for me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 305.01,
      "end_seconds": 306.6,
      "duration_seconds": 1.59,
      "text": "No guarding and no lumps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 308.04,
      "end_seconds": 309.58,
      "duration_seconds": 1.54,
      "text": "Bear with me a second."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 319.98,
      "end_seconds": 323.88,
      "duration_seconds": 3.9,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft, with mild tenderness in the upper middle part."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.78,
      "end_seconds": 349.55,
      "duration_seconds": 21.77,
      "text": "So, that's fine, you can get dressed. Thanks for bearing with me. Now that I've had a look, I can put the whole picture together. It's quite normal to feel unsure at this point. People often expect an instant answer, but a good assessment usually has a few stages, and today is mainly about narrowing things down and making a sensible plan together."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 350.22,
      "end_seconds": 351.86,
      "duration_seconds": 1.64,
      "text": "That's reassuring to hear."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 352.85,
      "end_seconds": 364.7,
      "duration_seconds": 11.85,
      "text": "Right, here's what I'm thinking. It fits best with gastritis. That's my thinking for now, and it may change as we learn more. It could also be acid reflux, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 365.19,
      "end_seconds": 369.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.37,
      "text": "I've been thinking the worst, to be honest. Is it bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 372.19,
      "end_seconds": 386.37,
      "duration_seconds": 14.18,
      "text": "I can't promise yet, but most people with gastritis do well once it's treated properly. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had a burning pain in the upper tummy for about a week, and no weight loss or fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 387.86,
      "end_seconds": 390.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.29,
      "text": "Exactly, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 391.43,
      "end_seconds": 395.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.71,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 396.57,
      "end_seconds": 409.79,
      "duration_seconds": 13.22,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 410.94,
      "end_seconds": 429.79,
      "duration_seconds": 18.85,
      "text": "We should do blood tests for dyspepsia. Avoid spicy, oily food and don't take anti-inflammatory painkillers on an empty stomach. Avoid taking any extra painkillers on top of what I'm prescribing without checking with us. Please don't sit on it if you vomit blood or pass black stools. That's the point to get seen urgently."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 430.98,
      "end_seconds": 432.69,
      "duration_seconds": 1.71,
      "text": "Got it, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 433.16,
      "end_seconds": 434.97,
      "duration_seconds": 1.81,
      "text": "Come back in four weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 436.19,
      "end_seconds": 436.89,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Alright."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 437.52,
      "end_seconds": 444.91,
      "duration_seconds": 7.39,
      "text": "Just so I know I've explained it clearly, can you tell me the plan back in your own words?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 445.9,
      "end_seconds": 450.1,
      "duration_seconds": 4.2,
      "text": "So, I come back in four weeks. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 451.04,
      "end_seconds": 454.38,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Yes, exactly right. Okay, we're done for today. Take care."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 454.77,
      "end_seconds": 457.1,
      "duration_seconds": 2.33,
      "text": "Alright, thanks. Bye for now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 458.15,
      "end_seconds": 459.29,
      "duration_seconds": 1.14,
      "text": "See you then."
    }
  ]
}